fh1-reimagined-arm64 builds Forza Horizon 1: ReImagined
(https://github.com/FH1-ReImagined/ForzaHorizon1-ReImagined, GPL-3.0-or-later with the
additional permission in its NOTICE.md) and its SDK ReIGlue
(https://github.com/FH1-ReImagined/ReIGlue, BSD-3-Clause) for linux-arm64. The patches in
this repository modify those projects and are released under the same licenses: patches/game
under GPL-3.0-or-later, patches/sdk under BSD-3-Clause.

The build also copies the native renderer and the shader tools of FH2 Recompiled
(https://github.com/gabrick75/fh2-recompiled, GPL-3.0; the renderer comes from
codepdbh/nfsmw-android and StevensND/nfsmw-nx, GPL-3.0, and the shader translator from
hedge-dev/XenosRecomp, MIT) into the game; patches/game adapts them to Forza Horizon
under GPL-3.0. scripts/fetch-toolchain.sh downloads DXC and SPIR-V Tools (Apache-2.0
with LLVM exceptions, and Apache-2.0) as built by fh2-recompiled-arm64.

